                <pb facs="0711" n="703" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg703"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60H31/148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-17T18:00:00-05:00">November 17, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Your 164, November 15, 6 p.m. (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) We have no
                    objection to a unilateral declaration as you propose, (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >b</hi>) Such a declaration might be given in the form of a memorandum.
                    However, (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) there should be no acknowledging
                    note.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
